apiVersion: kpt.dev/v1
kind: Kptfile
metadata:
  name: vlan-agent
  annotations:
    config.kubernetes.io/local-config: "true"
info:
  description: |
    VLAN agent for Nephio workload clusters.

    Automates the node-side VLAN sub-interface creation that the Nephio
    docs still require to be done manually (test-infra
    e2e/provision/hacks/vlan-interfaces.sh).

    Nephio's native networking flow is:
      Interface (attachmentType: vlan)
        -> VLANClaim (allocated by the vlan-specializer from a VLANIndex)
        -> NAD with master: <masterInterface>.<vlanID>   (generated by nad-fn)

    The macvlan CNI can only attach pods to <masterInterface>.<vlanID> if
    that VLAN sub-interface actually exists on the node. This DaemonSet
    watches the cluster's NetworkAttachmentDefinitions, extracts every
    master of the form "<nic>.<vlanID>", and creates/maintains those VLAN
    links on every node automatically. No manual script, no hardcoded
    VLAN range.

    Optionally, a static master-interface + vlan-range can be configured
    to pre-create VLANs exactly like the Nephio docs script does
    (eth1.2 ... eth1.6), in addition to the dynamic NAD discovery.

    Deploy this together with multus-cni, BEFORE any NF workloads, when
    using networking-mode "vlan".
  keywords:
    - nephio
    - vlan
    - networking
    - macvlan
    - multus
  site: https://nephio.org
pipeline:
  mutators:
    # Values come from vlan-setters.yaml so that PackageVariant setters are not
    # overwritten by blueprint defaults during rendering.
    - image: ghcr.io/kptdev/krm-functions-catalog/apply-setters:v0.2
      configPath: vlan-setters.yaml
